getting technical hands-on experience and general stimulation of
interest in their studies. For example, the Bi-Annual Solar Vehicle
Competition in Australia. (In this competition, teams of students
build vehicles powered by solar energy and race them.) I am
interested in any information regarding this type of
technologically-based competition.

2.      Computer simulators to assist learning and
demonstration of basic technical terms. I have heard of a computer
simulation of power plants that was devised to accompany a basic
course in thermodynamics.  At this time it is possible to pass a
basic course in thermodynamics with out knowing what a turbine
blade looks like.  Any type of computer simulator of relevance to
technical studies, such as those taught at the Technion, is of
interest to me.

